# EduGuard – Student Academic Early Warning System

## Project Overview

The Student Academic Early Warning System is an AI and Machine Learning-based web application designed to identify students who are at risk of poor academic performance before the final examination results are published.

The system analyzes important academic indicators such as attendance, internal assessment marks, assignment submissions, and classroom participation to predict students who may require additional academic support. By providing early alerts, the system helps faculty members take timely intervention measures to improve student performance and reduce failure rates.

---

## Problem Statement

College students often remain unaware of declining academic performance until examination results are published. Faculty members lack a unified mechanism to monitor attendance, assessment scores, and participation patterns simultaneously. An early warning system can help identify at-risk students and enable timely academic intervention.

---

## Objectives

- Predict students who are academically at risk.
- Monitor attendance and assessment performance.
- Analyze assignment submission patterns.
- Provide early alerts for faculty members.
- Support timely academic intervention.
- Improve overall student success and retention.

---

## Technologies Planned

- Frontend: HTML, CSS, JavaScript (or React)
- Backend: Python (Flask)
- Machine Learning: Scikit-learn, Pandas, NumPy
- Database: MySQL
- Version Control: Git & GitHub

